# Story 42: Running Vim & Htop (50s)
# Hook: vim, htop, less, nano -- full-screen programs just work, right inside a Rysh pane.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-042-running-vim-and-htop.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
vim, htop, less, nano -- full-screen programs just work, right inside a Rysh pane.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Start rysh -- a pane is a full PTY-backed shell.

[00:07.0 --> 00:14.0]
Open a file in vim. The moment vim switches to its alternate screen, Rysh detects it and enters raw mode automatically.

[00:14.0 --> 00:24.0]
Now every keystroke flows straight to the terminal emulator. Insert mode, normal mode -- vim behaves exactly as it should.

[00:24.0 --> 00:30.0]
Write and quit with colon-w-q. Back to the shell, no surprises.

[00:30.0 --> 00:40.0]
Run htop -- another alternate-screen program. Rysh's vt10x emulator renders the live process view inside the pane.

[00:40.0 --> 00:47.0]
Press q to quit htop and return to your shell prompt.

[00:47.0 --> 00:50.0]
Interactive terminal apps, no configuration, no caveats.

